# Mobile keyboard — LOCKED (reviewed Sep 2026)

**Product decision:** Native iOS keyboard with **blue checkmark** (bottom-right). **No toolbar / Done strip** above the keyboard. Same on Projects and Estimates.

Fixing one screen must **not** change keyboard behavior on another. Unless the user explicitly asks to change a **specific** field, do **not** touch keyboard props on unrelated inputs.

## Never do (causes grey key + cross-screen bleed)

- Mount `KeyboardPlainAccessory`, `KeyboardDoneAccessory`, `KeyboardDoneBar`, or any `InputAccessoryView` on **text** fields
- Add `inputAccessoryViewID` to text fields (numeric presets are native-pad-only — no accessory ID)
- Spread `blueDoneKeyboardProps` / `returnKeyType` / `blurOnSubmit` **before** other props (they get overridden → grey return)
- Combine `useKeyboard()` bottom padding + `automaticallyAdjustKeyboardInsets` + `KeyboardAvoidingView` on the same form
- Set iOS `keyboardDismissMode: 'on-drag'` on forms that use the blue checkmark (use `FORM_KEYBOARD_SCROLL_PROPS` or Estimates `keyboardDismissMode: 'none'`)
- Bulk-refactor keyboard props across a file when fixing one field

## Always do

| Field type | Implementation |
|---|---|
| **Single-line text** | `AppTextField` **or** `{...resolveTextInputKeyboardProps()}` spread **last** on raw `TextInput` |
| **Multiline notes** | `{...resolveTextInputKeyboardProps({ multiline: true })}` **last** |
| **Growing multiline** | `{...resolveTextInputKeyboardProps({ multiline: true, multilineMode: 'growable' })}` **last** |
| **Field chains** | Blue checkmark on every text field; use `onSubmitEditing` to focus the next ref (do **not** use grey `returnKeyType="next"`) |
| **Numeric** (`decimal-pad`, `phone-pad`) | `keyboardType` + `{...nativeNumericKeyboardProps}` only — dismiss via previous field’s checkmark, tap outside, or Save |
| **Project form scroll** | `{...FORM_KEYBOARD_SCROLL_PROPS}` on wrapping `ScrollView` / `FlatList` |

## Source of truth (edit behavior here only)

- `mobile/constants/inputKeyboardPresets.ts` — `resolveTextInputKeyboardProps`, `nativeNumericKeyboardProps`
- `mobile/constants/keyboardScrollProps.ts` — `FORM_KEYBOARD_SCROLL_PROPS`
- `mobile/components/ui/AppTextField.tsx` — labeled fields; calls `resolveTextInputKeyboardProps` internally

## Raw `TextInput` template

```tsx
<TextInput
  value={value}
  onChangeText={setValue}
  style={styles.input}
  placeholder="Vendor"
  onSubmitEditing={() => nextRef.current?.focus()}
  {...resolveTextInputKeyboardProps()}
/>

<ScrollView contentContainerStyle={…} {...FORM_KEYBOARD_SCROLL_PROPS}>
```

## Estimates

`estimate-generator.jsx` follows the same blue-checkmark contract. See `estimate-generator-keyboards-stable.mdc` for step-specific notes. Do not reintroduce `KeyboardPlainAccessory` on steps 1–2 or line-item modals.

## Before any keyboard edit

1. Grep the file for `KeyboardPlain`, `inputAccessoryViewID`, `returnKeyType`, `blueDoneKeyboardProps` — confirm only the intended field changed
2. Verify `resolveTextInputKeyboardProps` is the **last** spread on edited `TextInput`s
3. Do not change `inputKeyboardPresets.ts` / `keyboardScrollProps.ts` unless the contract itself must change (user approval)
